<Project>

  <!--
    Directory.Build.targets (Prowl user MSBuild customization)

    Like Directory.Build.props, Prowl never touches this file - but MSBuild imports it *after* the
    generated .csproj body, which is the only place we can remove items the generator added.
  -->

  <!--
    The tweening library is compiled from source out of Assets/Scripts/Tween. Prowl's project
    generator also adds a <Reference> to every assembly it finds in the engine build output, and
    that output still contains a stale Prowl.Tweening.dll from when this library lived in the
    engine repo. Both copies declare the same types, so every one of them collided (CS0436, ~370
    warnings) and the local source silently won.

    Dropping the reference here makes the local sources the single definition, and survives the
    .csproj being regenerated.

    If this library is ever moved back out of Assets - into the engine, or a shared project - delete
    this ItemGroup so the real assembly is referenced again.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <Reference Remove="Prowl.Tweening" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
